From e10dce10ae88529fafcfd1e7bd72cc296dc4f736 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:29:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shiro: objects shared with other Blink instances (shmobj):
 remote pages over the kernel's SharedArrayBuffer

A MAP_SHARED mapping of a /dev/shm file or a memfd asks the kernel for a
shared object (shiro_shmobj_map, 1020, remote at once: kind 0x100) and maps
shadow pages marked PAGE_REMOTE. No TLB caches them (nor the wasm JIT's:
compiled code leaves them to the interpreter), so every access comes through
LookupAddress2: an instruction locks the object, refreshes the page from the
buffer and writes it back when it ends (CommitStash, or the fault path); a
system call locks only around its copies and writes back what it changed.
FUTEX_WAIT/WAKE on such a word wait and wake on the buffer (Atomics), across
instances. munmap, exit and same-instance fork keep the kernel's mapping
counts. BLINK_SHMOBJ=0 maps such files as before.
---
